# Data Modeling Strategy

Rules for entities, DTOs, value objects, mappers, and database models.

## Requirements

- Must not pass API DTOs into domain logic or make UI depend on raw JSON.
- Must not use database table classes as UI state.
- Use immutable models for app state and domain entities.
- Keep mappers explicit and testable.
- Use value objects for important constrained values.
- Shape DTOs around external API contracts (`snake_case` JSON per [api-contract](../../.cursor/api-contract.mdc)).
- Shape entities around business meaning; keep presentation-only formatting out of entities.
- Entities and presentation models expose `human_friendly_id`; must not propagate raw table IDs to UI or domain contracts.

## Model types

| Type | Location | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| Entity | `domain/entities` | business meaning |
| Value object | `domain/value_objects` | validated values |
| DTO | `data/dtos` | API request/response shape |
| Database model | `data/datasources/local` | local persistence shape |
| View state | `presentation/state` | UI-ready state |

## Acceptance

- DTO-to-entity mapping is explicit.
- Invalid external data cannot silently become valid domain state.
- Tests cover important mappers and value objects.

